.TH DF 1V "6 March 1995"
.SH NAME
mklog \- create a log file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mklog 
[
.B \-help
]
[
.B \-version
]
.IR filename
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mklog
creates a new file by the specified name. If a file already exists with the 
specified name, that file is named by adding a numerical suffix to the files
name.  The numerical suffix is incremented until there is no longer a name
conflict.
.LP
In the following example a request is made for a new file with the name of
'foo'.  The existing 'foo' is given a numerical suffix which is incremented
until an unused name is found.  In this example the numerical suffix turns
out to be '3' (there already is a 'foo.1' and a 'foo.2').
.LP
.RS
.nf
.ft B
example% ls -l foo*
-rwxrwxr-x  1 example       18417 Jan 30 12:29 foo 
-rwxrwxr-x  1 example         735 Jan 30 12:29 foo.1
-rwxrwxr-x  1 example        9208 Jan 30 12:29 foo.2
example% mklog foo
example% ls -l foo*
-rwxrwxr-x  1 example           0 Jan 30 12:29 foo 
-rwxrwxr-x  1 example         735 Jan 30 12:29 foo.1
-rwxrwxr-x  1 example        9208 Jan 30 12:29 foo.2
-rwxrwxr-x  1 example       18417 Jan 30 12:29 foo.3
.ft R
.fi
.RE
.LP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-help
Print out a usage message and exit with status 0.
.TP
.B \-version
Report the CVS version number of the command invoked.
Print
.SH FILES
.PD 0
.TP 20
.B none
.PD
